# ACE agent demo — parameter file.
#
# Copy this file to `ace_agent.env` (same directory) and fill in your values.
# Both `ace_basic_demo.py` and `interactive_agent.py` auto-load it on startup —
# you do not need to export anything.
#
# Line format:  KEY=value     (optional `export ` prefix is tolerated)
# Comments:     anything after `#`
# Quotes:       values wrapped in "..." or '...' get stripped
#
# ─── SF connected-app config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Default auth (ContextAuth, JWT bearer) needs: SF_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH,
# SF_CONSUMER_KEY, SF_SUBJECT, SF_LOGIN_URL, BEACON_AGENT_ID, BEACON_OWNER_ID.
#
# `--user-login` auth (UserContextAuth.login(), OAuth + PKCE loopback) needs
# ONLY: SF_CONSUMER_KEY, SF_LOGIN_URL, BEACON_AGENT_ID. The private key,
# subject, and owner id are unused (owner is resolved from the signed-in user).

# Absolute path to the ECA Connected App private key (PEM). Keep this file
# out of git. Example: /Users/you/.secrets/jwt.key
# ── Default flow only; ignored with --user-login.
SF_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/absolute/path/to/jwt.key

# Connected App "Consumer Key" (aka client_id). Long base64-ish string.
# ── Required for both auth flows.
SF_CONSUMER_KEY=paste-your-consumer-key-here

# The Salesforce username the Connected App's JWT bearer flow is authorized
# to impersonate. Looks like an email.
# ── Default flow only; ignored with --user-login.
SF_SUBJECT=someuser@example.com

# My Domain / login host of the Salesforce org — host only, no https://.
# Example: acme.my.salesforce.com
# ── Required for both auth flows.
SF_LOGIN_URL=your-login-host.salesforce.com

# Beacon-registered agent id. Must exist on the target tenant.
# ── Required for both auth flows.
BEACON_AGENT_ID=TestAgent

# The end-user Salesforce id (18-char Individual id). The script passes this
# as the conversation owner and as the a360 `xid` in the token exchange.
# ── Default flow only; --user-login resolves it from the signed-in user.
BEACON_OWNER_ID=005xx000001X8UzAAK

# ─── Required for the LLM demos (interactive, quickstart, client_*) ────────
#
# Salesforce employees with the DevBar app installed can leave this as is:
# the demos fetch the current gateway key with `devbar auth claude`.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=paste-your-anthropic-api-key-here

# Optional. Anthropic-compatible endpoint; defaults to api.anthropic.com.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway-host/anthropic/v1

# Optional. Extra headers the gateway requires, one per line. Example:
#   ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS="x-example-header: value"
# ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS=

# Optional. Overrides the default model id (claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929).
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
